## Context

Fable 5.1 deep-QA pass (2026-09-06), verified against the actual installed
Zotero 10.0.1 source (`/opt/zotero7/app/omni.ja`), not assumptions.
`inspect()` (bootstrap.js) calls `await item.attachmentHash` -- a full,
uncached MD5 of the source file -- before its own cache lookup, because
the cache key embeds the hash. `sweep()` re-censuses the whole library on
every invocation, and the bootstrap wrapper reschedules a sweep 30s after
every sweep ends regardless of outcome (waiting, blocked, or error). Net
effect: continuous full-library disk I/O and CPU all night, every night,
directly contradicting the sitter's own "quiet supervisor, minimal
footprint" design ethos. Native Zotero's own SDT code already caches a
fingerprint keyed on (path, size, mtime) specifically to avoid this; the
sitter does not reuse it.

This is a plausible architectural contributor to the author's own
observed hang this morning ("stuck in a census loop") -- see ticket for
the heartbeat-blind-spot half of that story.

## Work

- Cache (path, size, mtime) per attachment identity alongside the existing
  pack-open cache record; skip the MD5 hash entirely when they match the
  last recorded values, matching native's own fingerprint discipline.
- Do not re-census on a fixed timer when the previous sweep ended
  `waiting` with zero candidates -- prefer reacting to a Zotero notifier
  event (new/changed attachment) over blind polling. If a fixed floor
  poll is kept for robustness, make its interval much longer than 30s
  when idle.
- Preserve the disposable-cache-only design (no durable ledger) --
  the fingerprint is derived/reconstructible, not a new persisted claim
  about job state.

## Acceptance

- [ ] A census with zero changed attachments performs zero new hash
      reads, verified by counting `attachmentHash`/`IOUtils` calls in a
      mock host across two consecutive sweeps with an unchanged library.
- [ ] An idle library (no candidates) does not re-census every 30s.
- [ ] Existing scheduler tests still pass unmodified in behavior for a
      library with actual changes.
